<title>USA: Qualcomm, Haitai in CDMA pact.</title>
<headline>Qualcomm, Haitai in CDMA pact.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qualcomm Inc said Monday it had granted Haitai Electronics Co Ltd. a multi-million dollar royalty-bearing license to make and sell wireless phones based on Qualcomm's Code Division Multiple Access (CDMA) technology.</p>
<p>Specific financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Haitai Electronics Co is part of the Haitai Group consisting of a total of 15 companies based in Seoul, Korea. Haitai Electronics has product lines including Vatel, Sherwood, Urban, INKEL, and Elger.</p>
</text>
